=== start ===
Andy: One of the volunteers remembers Keiko examining the watch with her students.
Farmer: Maybe she knows why it needed attention.
Andy: That's my thinking. But let's not jump to conclusions.
Keiko: Sheriff! What brings you here?
Andy: We're looking into something involving the Founders' Day display.
Keiko: Oh, the children are very excited about it. They've been preparing all week.
Farmer: Did they examine the old pocket watch?
Keiko: They did. We discovered it wasn't running. It gave us a wonderful opportunity to discuss how mechanical clocks work.
Andy: Did you happen to write a note about that?
Keiko: Yes, for the display preparations. I wanted to be certain it was attended to.
Andy: That's helpful. Thank you, Keiko.
Keiko returns to her class.
Andy: We know who noticed the problem. But we still don't know who moved the watch.
Farmer: Felix might know something. He handles a lot of the town's arrangements.
Andy: Worth asking.
Felix: Banners, tablecloths, display stands, replacement ribbon. Everyone remembers what they need at the last possible moment.
Andy: Sounds like you've been busy.
Felix: Busy is manageable. Unexpected is another matter.
+ [Ask Felix to check his repair ledger.]
    Farmer: Do you keep records of things sent away for repairs?
    Felix: Naturally. Every item has a date, a description, and a destination.
    Andy: Anything unusual this week?
    Felix: Let's see. One silver pocket watch, collected for servicing...
    -> solution
+ [Ask about recent display-related deliveries.]
    Farmer: Did anyone bring you something for the historical display?
    Felix: Several things. A cracked picture frame, two lamps, and a pocket watch.
    Andy: A pocket watch?
    Felix: Yes. Sent out for servicing yesterday.
    -> solution
+ [Show Felix the handwritten preparation note.]
    Farmer: Does this note look familiar?
    Felix: Ah, yes. Miss O'Brien mentioned the watch wasn't working. I arranged for a repair.
    Andy: You arranged a repair?
    Felix: Certainly. It was part of the approved preparations.
    -> solution
= solution
Andy: Felix, I believe you've just solved our missing-watch mystery.
Felix: Missing? The watch isn't missing. It's being repaired.
Andy: That's very good news. Unfortunately, nobody told the people responsible for the display.
Felix: I see. That would explain your interest.
Farmer: And Keiko thought the arrangements had been communicated.
Andy: Exactly. Let's make sure we've got the whole story.
Keiko joins them after school and confirms the celebration organizer approved the repair but did not update the display volunteers.
Keiko: Oh dear. I thought everyone knew. I wanted the children to hear it ticking again when they presented it.
Andy: And that's a fine idea. We just had a little confusion over where the watch had gone.
Felix: I have the receipt and the authorization right here.
Andy: Somehow, I expected you would.
Felix: The watch is running. The chain, however, is another matter.
Keiko: Can we still display it?
Andy: I think we've got one more little problem to solve.
-> END
=== complete ===
-> END
